## Why This Is Asked
Interview context explanation.

## Key Concepts
- systemd scopes and units
- CPUQuota, MemoryLimit, BlockIOWeight
- cgroup v2 basics vs v1
- rollback and safe testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js snippet to scaffold per-tenant scope units
const tenants = ["tenantA","tenantB"];
for (const t of tenants) {
  const unit = `[Unit]\nDescription=${t} scope\n\n[Scope]\nDescription=${t} per-tenant scope\n`;
  // would write to /etc/systemd/system/${t}.scope
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale this to dynamic tenant creation?
- What metrics would you surface to verify isolation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design isolation in software-defined networking within a Linux multi-tenant ingest stack, focusing on practical BPF/XDP, NIC tuning, and QoS.

## Key Concepts
- XDP/BPF for flow-level tenant routing
- Per-tenant queuing and pacing
- cgroups v2 IO control and CPU affinity
- NIC offloads and kernel tuning for latency

